    "turn_idx": 45,
    "turn_text": "I know you've put out a bipartisan product, but we'll talk about that in a second, but that's not even on the table right now. What's on the table is an asylum reform bill, a border security bill, with a number of pieces that I don't think anyone believed Joe Biden would support a year or two ago. But he seems to be the only person in Washington supporting this thing right now as Republicans abandoned it. Let's start with the politics of this bill. The conventional wisdom is Joe Biden is facing a very difficult re-election. Immigration is a top issue. Some polls say it even beats the economy in some of these polls, which is very rare. Most people think that's because of not unhappiness on the your side of the immigration issue, but coming from the right. And the White House political team believes that passing, moving to the right on immigration, passing this bill will not only, I assume they think it's good policy, but they think it will help them defeat Donald Trump. project you definitely support. Just unpack that political conversation as someone who has a foot in the Biden campaign as a co-chair and has your own strong views on immigration. Who's right?",
